{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1356 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b982610e0b5982a70bf2309c0b60cf41e2f7498030fb53f3974d676fbf76665c" :edb/db-before-t 1355 :edb/db-after-t 1356 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534668 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:44:12.661Z" 13194139534668 true] [17592186110591 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302409 13194139534668 true] [17592186110592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302395 13194139534668 true] [17592186110592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302402 13194139534668 true] [17592186110922 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534668 true] [17592186110922 1100 "$\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" 13194139534668 true] [17592186110922 1100 "What is $\\frac{\\tan θ \\cdot \\sec θ}{1 + \\tan^{2} θ}$?" 13194139534668 false] [17592186110922 1145 "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" 13194139534668 true] [17592186111279 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534668 true] [17592186111279 1100 "${sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=$" 13194139534668 true] [17592186111279 1100 "What is $\\sec^{2} x - 2\\tan^{2} x$?" 13194139534668 false] [17592186111279 1145 "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x & =1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x=1-{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302396 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1089 "q-120637" 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1100 "${tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1113 #uuid "88ef7ccf-542e-5c42-b011-ca1cd5a37425" 13194139534668 true] [17592186302395 1145 "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1+1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\